// EXPECT: E0253 — a name an imported module declares but does not export (ADR-0054 §2)
//
// `modules/Private.jr` puts `times_factor` and `unused_helper` behind `#scope_module`, so neither is
// in the scope this file resolves against.
//
// **Why this is not E0201.** The name genuinely is absent from the imported scope, so "unresolved
// name" would be *true* — and it would offer a near-name suggestion and send the reader looking for a
// typo. The difference between "you misspelled this" and "the module's author hid this" is the entire
// value of the diagnostic, and only the specific one can say it. That cost one extra lookup, on the
// error path only: the exported scope carries the set of names it filtered out.
#import "Private";

/// A hidden helper, used.
reach_private :: (n: s64) -> s64 {
    return times_factor(n);
}

/// A second one, to show the message names the module rather than the declaration.
reach_other :: (n: s64) -> s64 {
    return unused_helper(n);
}
